Exp-2 — Volumes & Snapshots
Volumes
a) Attach a Volume
Create an EC2, select an AZ.
Create a volume with the same AZ, size anything.
Attach volume to the running EC2, device name: /dev/sdf.
Open EC2 console and run lsblk.
b) Format and Mount the Volume
After attaching and connecting to EC2:

sudo su
lsblk -fs
fdisk /dev/nvme1n1    (m, n, p, , , , w)
lsblk
mkfs.xfs /dev/nvme1n1p1
mkdir /mnt/vish
mount /dev/nvme1n1p1 /mnt/vish
df -h
blkid /dev/nvme1n1p1
(COPY UUID)
nano /etc/fstab
(inside that, last line add) =UUID=<UUID-value>   /mnt/vish   xfs   defaults,nofail   0   0
mount -a
reboot and check for files
c) Move Volume to Another EC2
Create another EC2 with the same AZ.
Detach the volume from the old EC2 and attach to the new one.
Connect to the new EC2 and run:
sudo su
mkdir /mnt/vish
mount /dev/nvme1n1p1 /mnt/vish
lsblk -fs
Snapshots
For a given volume you created, click on Actions → Create Snapshot.
From the Snapshots section, click on Copy Snapshot and select some region.
Switch to that region and create a volume for it from Actions.
Attach an EC2 in that region to the created volume with the same AZ. (run lsblk if needed)



